<div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Editorial Policy</div><header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Transparency</span><h1>Editorial policy</h1><p>How we aim to make TechMintAI useful, accurate, readable and accountable.</p></header><div class="legal">
<h2>Reader-first content</h2><p>We publish explanations designed to answer a real question. Content should be original in presentation, organized around the reader’s intent, and clear about scope, limitations and assumptions. We avoid exaggerated earnings claims, guaranteed investment outcomes and unsupported “best” rankings.</p>
<h2>Sources and verification</h2><p>When appropriate we cite government bodies, regulators, official technical documentation and other reputable primary sources. Product claims and fast-changing information require checking against current official information before publication or substantial updates. External references in articles point to background sources; they do not mean the entire article has been independently endorsed.</p>
<h2>AI-assisted drafting</h2><p>AI tools may assist research organization, outlines or early drafting. AI output can be inaccurate, and should not be treated as a verified source. Our standard is to fact-check claims and links before publication, especially for financial, medical, legal and security-sensitive topics. Our current starter articles should be reviewed by the publisher before promoting them as expert-reviewed.</p>
<h2>Updates and corrections</h2><p>Publication dates indicate initial publication. We add a substantive “Updated” date only when an article is materially revised. We aim to correct clear factual errors promptly and transparently. Readers can flag an issue using our <a href="/contact/">contact details</a>.</p>
<h2>Commercial independence</h2><p>Advertising and affiliate programs may fund TechMintAI. We mark sponsored content and disclose affiliate relationships when present. Payment should not determine the factual conclusions of an editorial article. We do not sell favorable reviews disguised as independent coverage.</p>
<h2>Calculators</h2><p>Calculators are educational estimates. We disclose assumptions and do not use user-entered numbers as financial advice. Always compare estimates with actual product terms, fees and local regulations.</p></div></div>
</Base>
